# Deny everything, then allow only what the build needs.
#
# The leading `*` is the whole point of this file's shape. A new file at the repository root
# - a scratch script, a second .env, a colleague's notebook - is excluded by DEFAULT and can
# only enter the build context by someone deliberately adding it below. An allowlist of
# denials cannot give that property: it protects only against the files someone thought of.
#
# Second, independent barrier: the Dockerfile never uses `COPY . .`. Every COPY names an
# explicit path. So a mistake in this file alone cannot leak anything into an image; it would
# take two independent mistakes.
#
# What this keeps out, specifically, and why it matters: `.env` holds live API keys;
# `memory/portfolio.json` holds the author's actual stock holdings and share counts;
# `memory/candidates.json` and `memory/rates.json` hold their candidate pools and remembered
# rates; `output/` holds their generated portfolio reports; `data/holdings.duckdb` is a price
# cache for only the tickers they personally own. None of that belongs in a published image.
*

!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md
!LICENSE
!NOTICE
!src/
!docker/

# data/ must be un-ignored for Docker to traverse into it, then its contents re-denied, so
# that exactly one file can be re-admitted by name. `portfolio.duckdb` is market data and is
# the bundled dataset. `holdings.duckdb` is personal (see above). `news_archive_source.parquet`
# is 9.2 MB whose contents are already materialized into the news table inside
# `portfolio.duckdb`, so shipping it would waste space for nothing.
!data/
data/*
!data/portfolio.duckdb

# Re-deny build artifacts inside otherwise-allowed directories.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
